<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Authors>SplatDev</Authors>
    <Company>SplatDev Ltda</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) SplatDev Ltda 2026</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/SplatDev-Ltda/SplatDev.Umbraco.Plugins</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/SplatDev-Ltda/SplatDev.Umbraco.Plugins</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    MailKit/MimeKit were previously declared here, which made every one of the ~155
    projects inherit them. Only SplatDev.Umbraco.Plugins.Mailer actually uses them, and it
    already declares its own reference.

    Two concrete problems that caused:
      1. Every published package listed MailKit + MimeKit as dependencies (once per target
         framework), so installing any SplatDev plugin dragged in an email stack it never
         used. It also broke restore in environments with a restricted package source.
      2. The 4.17.0 pinned here silently overrode Mailer's own 4.15.1, so the version the
         project asked for was not the version it got.

    Add a PackageReference to the project that needs it, not to every project in the repo.
  -->
</Project>
